	(uuid "9c8ca51d-f5a2-41c9-bd6b-e1ed60a7586f")
	(paper "A4")
	(title_block
		(title "MCU Test PCB for PID Loop Development")
		(date "2025-12-24")
		(rev "1.1")
		(company "JRDish")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "STATUS INDICATOR\n\nPin	Signal	Label	Function	Config\n21	PA12	STATUS_LED	GPIO_Output	Push-pull, starts LOW\nLED: Active-high with current-limiting resistor\n\nUART (TTL 3.3V - MODBUS RTU)\n\nPin	Signal	Function	Config\n28	PB6	USART1_TX	Transmit, 115200 baud\n29	PB7	USART1_RX	Receive, 115200 baud\nProtocol: Modbus RTU over TTL UART (no RS-485 transceiver)\n\nDEBUG (SWD + SWO)\n\nPin	Signal	Function	Config\n22	PA13	SWDIO	SWD data\n23	PA14	SWCLK	SWD clock\n25	PB3	SWO	Debug trace output (optional)\nConnector: 2×5 pin 1.27mm (0.05\") SWD header\n\nUNUSED/AVAILABLE\n\nPin	Signal	Status\n15	PA5	Available\n24	PA15	Available\n26	PB4	Available\n30	PB9	Available\n2	PC13	Available (also RTC/Wakeup)\n3	PC14	Available (also OSC32_IN)\n4	PC15	Available (also OSC32_OUT)\nPeripheral Summary\nPeripheral	Function	Pins	Configuration\nTIM2	Encoder Interface	PA0, PA1, PA2	32-bit quadrature, 4× resolution\nTIM3	PWM Generation	PB0	10 kHz, prescaler=16, period=999\nTIM6	Microsecond Timer	-	1 µs resolution, prescaler=169\nUSART1	Modbus RTU	PB6, PB7	115200 baud, 8N1, TTL level\nI2C3	Sensor/EEPROM Bus	PA8, PB5	100/400 kHz, hardware I2C\nGPIO	Various I/O	Multiple	See tables above\nClock Configuration\nHSE:     16 MHz (external crystal)\nPLL:     ÷4 → ×85 → ÷2\nSYSCLK:  170 MHz\nHCLK:    170 MHz\nAPB1:    170 MHz\nAPB2:    170 MHz\nAddress Configuration (Backplane)\nSlot	ADDR2	ADDR1	ADDR0	Binary	Address	Function\n1	+3V	+3V	+3V	000	0x01	Azimuth\n2	+3V	+3V	GND	001	0x02	Elevation\n3	+3V	GND	+3V	010	0x03	Polarizer\n4	+3V	GND	GND	011	0x04	Focus\n5	GND	+3V	+3V	100	0x05	Spare\n6	GND	+3V	GND	101	0x06	Spare\n7	GND	GND	+3V	110	0x07	Spare\n8	GND	GND	GND	111	0x08	Spare\n\nDuring operation speed and position commands are received over \nthe USART from the Raspberry Pi.\nMCU outputs pulse and direction signals to the motor controller.\nLimit switches disable movement in the limit switched direction.\nMCU reads position with the encoder inputs.\nMCU has a PID loop to maintain speed and position.\n\nThe 3.3V for the MCU is from the LD39050PU33R converting 5V\n from the Pi 5V pin to 3.3V.\n\nThe PI and MCU circuitry is protected from the IO circuitry \nby using LTV-8x7S isolator chips.\n\nThe I2C sensors are not isolated from the MCU.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.11 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8f6652cc-3bb6-47f9-a628-17b80adc2590")
	)
	(text "Custom PCB definition\n\nMCU is the STM32G431KBT6TR, 32-pin LQFP48 package\nSpeed and position connands are received from a Raspberry Pi over the USART.\nEncoder is the E6B2-CWZ6C.\nMotor Controller: DM556Y.\n2-Wire program/debug connector with SWO.\nI2C for reading I2C sensors.\n2 Limit switches.\nUSART communication to Raspberry Pi.\nBoot0 and NRST connects to raspberry pi to enable firmware update orver USART.\n16MHz oscillator, prescalers configures for 170MHz.\n\nThe STM32G474 datasheet is at https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/stm32g431c6.pdf\nSee table 12 in the datasheet for the STM32G413 pinouts for the LQFP32 package.\n\n\nMCU Specifications\nPart Number: STM32G431KBT6TR\nPackage: LQFP32 (7×7mm, 0.8mm pitch)\nClock: 170 MHz (16 MHz crystal + PLL)\nFlash: 128 KB\nRAM: 32 KB\nPin Assignments by Function\nPOWER & SYSTEM\n\nPin	Signal	Function	Notes\n1	VDD	+3.3V Power	Decouple with 100nF + 10µF\n9	VDDA	Analog +3.3V	Decouple with 100nF + 10µF\n17	VDD	+3.3V Power	Decouple with 100nF\n8	VSSA	Analog Ground	-\n32	VSS	Ground	-\n7	NRST	Reset	10kΩ pull-up to VDD\n31	BOOT0	Boot Mode	10kΩ pull-down to GND\nCLOCK (16 MHz CRYSTAL)\n\nPin	Signal	Function	Notes\n5	PF0	OSC_IN	HSE input, 16 MHz crystal\n6	PF1	OSC_OUT	HSE output, 16 MHz crystal\nCrystal: 16 MHz, 10pF load caps (C0G/NP0)\n\nENCODER INTERFACE (TIM2 - 32-BIT)\n\nPin	Signal	Label	Function	Config\n10	PA0	ENC_A	TIM2_CH1	Encoder A channel\n11	PA1	ENC_B	TIM2_CH2	Encoder B channel\n12	PA2	ENC_Z	GPIO_EXTI2	Z/Index pulse, rising edge interrupt, pull-up\nMode: Quadrature encoder, 32-bit counter, 4× resolution\n\nLIMIT SWITCHES\n\nPin	Signal	Label	Function	Config\n13	PA3	LIMIT_SW1	GPIO_Input	Pull-up enabled\n14	PA4	LIMIT_SW2	GPIO_Input	Pull-up enabled\nCircuit: Normally-open switches to GND\n\nMOTOR CONTROL\n\nPin	Signal	Label	Function	Config\n15	PA6	ENABLE	GPIO_Output	Push-pull, starts LOW\n16	PA7	DIR	GPIO_Output	Push-pull, starts LOW\n17	PB0	PWM	TIM3_CH3	10 kHz PWM output\nPWM: 10 kHz, 0-999 duty cycle range (0-100%)\n\nI2C3 (SENSORS/EEPROM)\n\nPin	Signal	Function	Config\n27	PA8	I2C3_SCL	I2C clock, 100/400 kHz\n23	PB5	I2C3_SDA	I2C data, open-drain\nRequired: External 4.7kΩ pull-ups on both SCL and SDA to +3.3V\n\nAUTO-ADDRESSING (3-BIT)\n\nPin	Signal	Label	Function	Config\n18	PA9	ADDR0	GPIO_Input	LSB, pull-up enabled\n19	PA10	ADDR1	GPIO_Input	Mid bit, pull-up enabled\n20	PA11	ADDR2	GPIO_Input	MSB, pull-up enabled\nAddress Range: 0x01 to 0x08 (addresses 1-8) Backplane: Overrides with +3.3V or GND per slot\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 104.14 0)
